    "when": {
      "flagsAll": [
        "soldier_read",
        "clergyman_read"
      ],
      "personsPresent": [
        "holmes"
      ]
    },
    "once": true,
    "effects": [
      {
        "kind": "playBeat",
        "beats": [
          "The light was going, and Holmes had gone back to the window.",
          "\"You did very well, Watson. Better than you know.\"",
          "He asked me to describe any one of the some hundreds who had passed under the window since I began, one he had not pointed out. I could not: not one face.",
          "\"Nor could I. Nor could any constable on any beat in London. We see what asks to be seen. A man who asks nothing of anybody, who dresses as the street dresses and walks as the street walks, might pass under this window every evening for a year and never once be looked at.\""
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "grantFact",
        "person": "player",
        "fact": "holmes_invisible_in_a_crowd",
        "from": "holmes"
      },
      {
        "kind": "setFlag",
        "flag": "closing_heard"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "soldier_verdict_right",
