    "when": {
      "personsPresent": [
        "holmes"
      ]
    },
    "once": true,
    "effects": [
      {
        "kind": "playBeat",
        "beats": [
          "When he had done, I called it a very good parlour trick. Holmes turned from the window with a look I had learned, in seven years, to distrust.",
          "\"Very well,\" he said. \"A wager.\" Two people in the street below, to be read correctly.",
          "\"Tell me when you have him. I shall hold you to your first answer.\"",
          "He gestured at the window: the old fellow on the kerb by the cab rank, just under the window, and the clergyman across the street outside the chemist's, his face half-lost under the brim of his hat.",
          "\"Take your time. I have nothing whatever else to do.\""
        ]
      },
      {
